  questions  to see what that would look like and  then you can also click on the student  view to see what this what it will look  like for the student  another thing on the assignments is that  i've had a lot of teachers  who  don't necessarily  for whatever reason they don't like  looking through  that the entire list for a specific  thing that they know that they want to  assign so they will use the search bar  up at the very top  and  they may search  quadratic yeah quadratic equations and  once they find so they know exactly what  they want to assign to their students  they just need to find it and they'll  use that search bar they'll find the  exercise that they want to use  and they will click on it  and i've used this quite often too the  tab at the top now allows you to assign  that specific assignment to the to  students through that method once you  see it on your screen once you see the  student view on your screen um so you  can still have the same options and  assign it that direct in that way  i love that because i feel like it can  be totally overwhelming to look at that  massive list of skills and videos on the  course but if you just want one skill or  one video  search for that thing you want and then  click the blue bar to go right to the  assignment piece  okay i know we're running out of time so  i want to finish up with three questions  starting with a really great one that i  received from rose an eighth grader so  again these webinars are promoted very  broadly um rose says i'm an eighth  grader who's getting ready for high  school next year and i'm worried with  this whole thing happening  you know in school being closed how can  i be ready how can i prepare  as a high school teacher speaking to a  future high schooler what advice would  you give rose for really making sure  she's ready for prime time hopefully  knock on wood come september  yeah well first i would say rose could  you uh if you want to move to northwest  georgia and come to my classroom it  sounds like you're a great student so  that that is awesome but you're  concerned with it but uh using khan  academy  my suggestion would be to go into the  the courses in the top left hand corner  and choose uh  that you know in our school we move into  algebra one so if you're moving into  algebra one uh select the course that  you were wanting to do  or that you're going to be moving into  and begin  begin at that first unit and and work  your way through it uh  use the videos as a help like i said i  started with khan academy with the on  the on youtube and uh using videos to  help me  kind of solidify the things that i was  hearing in class but even as a first  instruction uh those videos they're  great instructional videos and i highly  recommend them uh to walk watch through  them and then practice your exercises  and one thing that we have not touched  on is the um  the mastery challenges that are are  somewhat new to khan academy  so whenever you click on that course  page  at the top you will receive a mastery  challenge a lot of times i have my  students do that  maybe as a warm-up when they come in in  the morning  or uh throughout the day when they  finish an assignment to go work on their  course math their mastery challenge and  this is just a spiral review for all the  things that you have covered to uh just  re-revisit and make sure you've not  forgotten the things that you have done  through on khan academy  all right great advice for rose and  rosie wish you good luck i know it's a  hard time right now but thank you for  joining us and um i have a feeling that  they're awesome mr culver's in your  future in high school so more support to  come  um second question for you matt is i  know we haven't been able to cover every  question that came in right now  if educators are still hungry for  answers after the session where would  you recommend they go next  so a couple of different places that  that i would say one is um  first i would say under on your teacher  dashboard i've directed a lot of  teachers this uh  to this point is the resources tab  and there's a lot of good videos  underneath that resources tab especially  for getting started um so if you're  really new to it and you want to look at  some different things you know check  check all of those out  if you run into like a specific question  or something that you need to ask  underneath your name in the top right  hand corner  there is when you click on it there is a  help  help section so you can click on that  help section and your  questions are sent directly to  khan academy experts who who get back to  you quite quickly  you just have to report the problem at  the top  and i've had good experience with that  the last area that i would recommend  everyone joining is a facebook page and  it is khan academy for teachers  and and i'm a member there and uh tend  to  i look at it almost daily and uh just  see some of the conversations that are  going on there but there are a  bajillion uh great khan academy teachers  that use khan academy on there that can  answer a lot of great questions a lot of  questions that you have  all right awesome i'm just sharing all  those resources in the chat so if you  want to get the resources if you want to  get the request help from khan academy  or join the facebook group all that is  in your chat and then lastly that i know  that you've already shared a ton but if  you have any final words of wisdom for  educators out there across the country  as we're thinking about oh my goodness  i've got at least a couple more weeks to  go probably many more than that  how do i make the most of this time how  do i support my students and their  families  any sort of stage advice you can share  i have just one tried to not get  overwhelmed by it all you know make sure  you're taking care of yourself and  taking care of uh  your immediate family first because  if you are not in good health and  there's no way you can help anyone else  so take care of yourself but two just  try to keep it some sort of a  communication line open with your  students i think that is uh the most  important thing that students can know  that you are there that you are  available to them and um  and the content will start to once they  have that relationship and they they  know that you're you're looking out for  their best interest the the content side  of it starts to kind of fall in place  i love that yeah it's almost like the  advice you give to new parents you've  got to take care of yourself before you  can take care of your kids and the same  is doubly true for educators  so absolutely um  matt has given us tons of new wisdom  to pursue these big challenges we have  ahead of us it's also given us the  strength to do it um at a time when we  need it the most so i want to thank you  matt for sharing all your expertise  today and i want to thank everyone out  there listening in for investing in the  session and i wish you tremendous  success in the weeks to come thank you  so much and have a great weekend all  thank you all
 

